      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "108 women aged 28 to 74 years underwent cardiac angiography for evaluation of chest pain or other heart disease. 29 were found to be free of coronary disease and formed a control group. Multi-variable analysis indicated that hypercholesterolemia, hypertension, familial coronary disease and diabetes were the most relevant atherogenic risk factors."},
